WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:44.087
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:44.357 --> 00:48.069
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

3
01:42.957 --> 01:45.126
‎EPISODE 1

4
01:46.794 --> 01:49.005
‎How much does ‎tangsuyuk‎ cost these days?

5
01:50.256 --> 01:52.717
‎How will you ever pay off your debt

6
01:53.384 --> 01:55.011
‎and live independently at this rate?

7
01:59.265 --> 02:00.183
‎Yes!

8
02:01.100 --> 02:03.019
‎That's how you do it!

9
02:04.020 --> 02:06.856
‎I don't know how to lose.

10
02:06.940 --> 02:09.359
‎Man, she's so damn loud.

11
02:12.278 --> 02:14.906
‎Hey, mister. Change out the lights!

12
02:17.242 --> 02:20.119
‎Want to go against her? ‎I'll clean her out, down to her underwear.

13
02:20.203 --> 02:22.664
‎Man, even I can't wear something that big.

14
02:24.207 --> 02:27.252
‎Sir, can we get ‎tangsuyuk‎ and ‎jjajangmyeon‎?

15
02:28.086 --> 02:28.920
‎Fine.

16
02:29.504 --> 02:30.838
‎Make those extra-large!

17
02:33.174 --> 02:35.551
‎Goodness, a doctor-turned-mayor.

18
02:35.635 --> 02:38.805
‎As head of the Seonam Medical Association, ‎I'm thrilled, Mr. Mayor.

19
02:39.472 --> 02:41.849
‎This is all thanks to you, President Kim.

20
02:41.933 --> 02:42.850
‎Not at all.

21
02:44.102 --> 02:47.230
‎My dear Mr. Mayor, ‎I hope you won't forget me,

22
02:47.313 --> 02:50.149
‎Director Kim Myeong-seop, ‎and Guseo University Medical Center too.

23
02:52.568 --> 02:54.612
‎I could never forget you, Director.

24
03:04.998 --> 03:06.499
‎Congratulations, Mr. Mayor.

25
03:08.084 --> 03:09.002
‎Thank you.

26
03:11.337 --> 03:14.507
‎Gosh, why are you pouring wine like soju?

27
03:14.590 --> 03:16.300
‎You're sure in a celebratory mood.

28
03:17.385 --> 03:19.178
‎-Mayor Im Ho-seok. ‎-Yes?

29
03:19.262 --> 03:21.389
‎This is Dr. Do Yun-sik from GUMC.

30
03:23.683 --> 03:26.060
‎Oh, yes. I enjoyed your latest paper.

31
03:26.144 --> 03:28.855
‎Your clinical research is exceptional.

32
03:28.938 --> 03:31.774
‎It's all thanks to Director Kim ‎and Chairman Gu.

33
03:31.858 --> 03:33.151
‎-Pour me a glass. ‎-Yes, sir.

34
03:34.652 --> 03:35.820
‎-Not too much. ‎-Yes, sir.

35
03:36.404 --> 03:39.115
‎-Chairman Gu, I'm Jung Geon-hui. ‎-Right.

36
03:39.198 --> 03:40.908
‎Chairman Gu, I'm Kim Gwang-hyeon.

37
03:40.992 --> 03:42.118
‎Okay.

38
03:42.201 --> 03:44.203
‎-Sir, I'm Lee Gyeong-seok. ‎-All right.

39
03:45.913 --> 03:48.583
‎Go into plastics or dermatology. ‎Why general surgery?

40
03:49.542 --> 03:51.919
‎-Or how about ophthalmology? ‎-Let him be.

41
03:52.003 --> 03:54.047
‎It's good to know a surgeon ‎when you get older.

42
03:54.881 --> 03:56.257
‎So how about orthopedics?

43
03:56.341 --> 03:58.343
‎In that case, why not internal medicine?

44
03:58.426 --> 04:01.012
‎I didn't go to med school for you guys.

45
04:01.095 --> 04:03.723
‎Right. ‎You went to inherit the family practice.

46
04:03.806 --> 04:05.933
‎Just shoot some pool, you punks.

47
04:11.272 --> 04:13.441
‎Crazy bastard. What are you, a pervert?

48
04:13.983 --> 04:15.902
‎I grazed it with the cue stick earlier.

49
04:16.903 --> 04:18.279
‎I need to go to the restroom.

50
04:18.363 --> 04:19.197
‎Hurry up.

51
04:26.621 --> 04:28.498
‎-What's wrong? Hey! ‎-It hurts!

52
04:28.581 --> 04:30.375
‎Sir, are you okay?

53
04:30.458 --> 04:31.626
‎Where does it hurt?

54
04:31.709 --> 04:34.003
‎Right here.

55
04:36.381 --> 04:38.549
‎Is it swollen? What is this part called?

56
04:52.438 --> 04:53.523
‎Are you a doctor too?

57
05:01.781 --> 05:03.741
‎I… I'm an intern.

58
05:05.618 --> 05:06.786
‎Get him up. Now.

59
05:06.869 --> 05:07.703
‎Okay.

60
05:11.916 --> 05:13.126
‎It hurts.

61
05:13.209 --> 05:14.794
‎I'm going to have to undress you.

62
05:14.877 --> 05:16.129
‎Lady, are you insane?

63
05:17.880 --> 05:19.465
‎-You want your friend to die? ‎-Damn it.

64
05:20.341 --> 05:21.384
‎Cough for me.

65
05:22.718 --> 05:23.761
‎Tighten your stomach.

66
05:24.262 --> 05:25.221
‎Cough.

67
05:33.855 --> 05:36.315
‎It's a left inguinal hernia. ‎I performed a manual reduction.

68
05:37.525 --> 05:39.235
‎Oh, an inguinal hernia…

69
05:39.318 --> 05:41.571
‎There's a risk of recurrence. ‎He needs emergency surgery.

70
05:41.654 --> 05:43.072
‎You're a doctor, right? Come with us.

71
05:46.576 --> 05:48.077
‎But I'm an intern.

72
05:49.036 --> 05:50.371
‎Wait a minute!

73
05:52.415 --> 05:54.125
‎Can I at least get your name?

74
05:57.086 --> 05:59.881
‎We fought through the COVID-19 pandemic,

75
05:59.964 --> 06:02.508
‎the CCTV mandate in operating rooms,

76
06:02.592 --> 06:04.385
‎and strikes over medical school quotas.

77
06:04.927 --> 06:06.179
‎We've managed to endure

78
06:07.138 --> 06:09.390
‎this grueling ordeal ‎with everything we had.

79
06:10.808 --> 06:12.226
‎But the crisis isn't over.

80
06:12.310 --> 06:14.061
‎We face union struggles from within,

81
06:14.145 --> 06:15.897
‎Medical Service Act reforms ‎from the outside,

82
06:15.980 --> 06:19.483
‎and the media paints us as frauds.

83
06:20.401 --> 06:22.570
‎Protecting doctors is the only way

84
06:22.653 --> 06:24.780
‎to set healthcare right, but those…

85
06:28.784 --> 06:30.703
‎Those fools fail to see it.

86
06:31.412 --> 06:32.413
‎Now more than ever,

87
06:33.789 --> 06:36.500
‎Magnolia must unite.

88
06:37.418 --> 06:39.503
‎The election ‎of our very own Mayor Im Ho-seok

89
06:40.504 --> 06:41.923
‎is just the beginning.

90
06:54.060 --> 06:56.395
‎Well said, sir!

91
06:57.605 --> 06:58.689
‎All right.

92
06:59.607 --> 07:00.900
‎I swear before the white coat

93
07:00.983 --> 07:02.985
‎never to forget where I started.

94
07:03.611 --> 07:05.112
‎And I'll never forget

95
07:05.613 --> 07:08.532
‎the proactive support from Magnolia!

96
07:09.659 --> 07:10.701
‎Everyone,

97
07:10.785 --> 07:12.662
‎here's to the white coat!

98
07:13.204 --> 07:14.830
‎-Cheers! ‎-Cheers!

99
07:35.685 --> 07:37.103
‎Yet another resignation?

100
07:37.186 --> 07:38.813
‎I'm going to lose it.

101
07:39.522 --> 07:40.648
‎They're not answering?

102
07:42.650 --> 07:43.734
‎Hey, let's talk more later.

103
07:46.487 --> 07:47.905
‎Why did you come out?

104
07:51.951 --> 07:52.785
‎You work too hard.

105
07:53.869 --> 07:55.746
‎No, please go back inside.

106
07:55.830 --> 07:58.082
‎I need to use the restroom.

107
08:02.962 --> 08:04.255
‎No more wine, sir.

108
08:06.007 --> 08:09.010
‎You should be protecting patients, ‎you goddamn bastards.

109
08:10.219 --> 08:13.097
‎I hope you all get gout ‎after eating all that meat.

110
08:14.390 --> 08:16.267
‎Is there even a doctor worth protecting?

111
08:18.227 --> 08:19.437
‎You bastards.

112
08:22.481 --> 08:24.150
‎Wow, this is insane.

113
08:24.650 --> 08:26.861
‎I've never taken someone to the ER ‎after a manual reduction.

114
08:28.070 --> 08:29.864
‎I've never seen this before either.

115
08:31.741 --> 08:32.992
‎Wait a minute!

116
08:35.661 --> 08:37.330
‎Can I at least get your name?

117
08:41.292 --> 08:42.293
‎What?

118
08:42.960 --> 08:43.961
‎What's that?

119
08:44.045 --> 08:45.713
‎What does that mean?

120
08:45.796 --> 08:47.715
‎Who are you?

121
08:55.139 --> 08:57.642
‎The white tower is collapsing.

122
08:59.352 --> 09:02.897
‎Through the COVID-19 pandemic, ‎the CCTV mandate in operating rooms,

123
09:04.065 --> 09:06.859
‎and the strikes over med school quotas,

124
09:07.443 --> 09:09.111
‎hospitals faced constant turmoil.

125
09:09.195 --> 09:10.946
‎SURGERY-RELATED DEPARTMENTS ‎WILL SHARE STAFF ROOM

126
09:11.030 --> 09:13.574
‎They started construction a while ago.

127
09:15.910 --> 09:17.578
‎But I don't see any progress.

128
09:18.287 --> 09:19.288
‎Damn it.

129
09:20.247 --> 09:24.126
‎The government pushed ‎a half-baked bill for show,

130
09:24.210 --> 09:27.380
‎and doctors responded by walking out.

131
09:28.631 --> 09:30.758
‎As the conflict intensifies, ‎patients are overlooked.

132
09:31.592 --> 09:33.219
‎First doctors, and now nurses?

133
09:33.302 --> 09:35.096
‎I know working in surgery is grueling,

134
09:35.179 --> 09:37.098
‎but how did you let this happen?

135
09:37.682 --> 09:39.183
‎-Sorry, sir. ‎-I'm sorry.

136
09:40.017 --> 09:41.769
‎I'm making rounds ‎for the first time in ages.

137
09:41.852 --> 09:43.270
‎I'm going to lose face over this.

138
09:43.354 --> 09:44.730
‎What about the OR?

139
09:47.817 --> 09:49.068
‎Well…

140
09:49.151 --> 09:51.445
‎I did find someone on short notice

141
09:52.029 --> 09:53.781
‎to help out temporarily…

142
09:53.864 --> 09:57.201
‎GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

143
10:04.458 --> 10:05.459
‎Then…

144
10:06.085 --> 10:08.379
‎a new kind of doctor appeared.

145
10:09.463 --> 10:11.298
‎One who belongs to no group.

146
10:17.930 --> 10:20.015
‎Hello, I'm your new surgical intern!

147
10:20.099 --> 10:21.934
‎My name is Park Tae-gyeong!

148
10:22.017 --> 10:23.060
‎I'm excited to work with you!

149
10:30.359 --> 10:31.652
‎Excuse me, am I late?

150
10:32.903 --> 10:34.029
‎No, I'm not.

151
10:35.781 --> 10:37.700
‎Sir, can I ask you a question?

152
10:39.785 --> 10:41.996
‎Hi, I'm Ma Seong-gyu, ‎your senior resident.

153
10:42.079 --> 10:43.038
‎Nice to meet you.

154
10:43.122 --> 10:45.791
‎I should be nicer to you, ‎but I don't have the capability

155
10:45.875 --> 10:48.461
‎because the director just called rounds,

156
10:48.544 --> 10:50.796
‎which means you need to ‎get out there right now.

157
10:51.297 --> 10:52.339
‎You can sit…

158
10:53.507 --> 10:55.092
‎Not that you'd choose general surgery…

159
10:56.093 --> 10:58.971
‎Just sit wherever.

160
10:59.054 --> 11:00.848
‎But don't quit this week.

161
11:03.350 --> 11:05.269
‎-What are you doing, intern? ‎-What?

162
11:06.228 --> 11:07.062
‎Oh, rounds.

163
11:07.146 --> 11:08.063
‎Yes, sir!

164
11:14.236 --> 11:17.615
‎Director Kim Myeong-seop ‎will now begin rounds.

165
11:21.827 --> 11:24.205
‎A freelancer unattached ‎to any hospital department.

166
11:24.288 --> 11:26.207
‎Also known as a mercenary doctor.

167
11:27.458 --> 11:30.878
‎This is the story of a lone wolf.

168
11:31.462 --> 11:36.258
‎A solitary figure that has emerged ‎in the era of mafia in white,

169
11:36.342 --> 11:40.221
‎where even the practice of saving lives ‎is driven by money and power.

170
11:41.388 --> 11:43.140
‎This person right here

171
11:44.058 --> 11:47.311
‎despises authority and answers to no one.

172
11:47.811 --> 11:49.813
‎Her only weapons are her medical license

173
11:49.897 --> 11:53.484
‎and the surgical skills ‎she has honed from the bottom up.

174
11:54.318 --> 11:56.278
‎Meet Gye Su-jeong, a surgeon.

175
11:56.779 --> 11:58.030
‎Also known as

176
11:58.614 --> 12:00.407
‎Doctor X.

177
12:13.212 --> 12:15.548
‎I haven't had a chance ‎to look at your file yet.

178
12:15.631 --> 12:16.966
‎What's your name?

179
12:19.677 --> 12:20.761
‎Gye Su-jeong.

180
12:27.977 --> 12:30.104
‎Your last name is "Gye"? That's unusual.

181
12:34.900 --> 12:37.778
‎There's a pre-op conference today,

182
12:37.861 --> 12:38.904
‎so attend that first.

183
12:40.864 --> 12:41.824
‎You…

184
12:41.907 --> 12:42.992
‎Dr. Gye.

185
12:43.075 --> 12:46.287
‎You need to verbally respond ‎when he talks to you.

186
12:47.413 --> 12:50.249
‎-Director Kim is waiting. Please hurry. ‎-Oh my.

187
12:59.258 --> 13:02.428
‎Director Kim seems really pumped.

188
13:02.511 --> 13:04.346
‎He's even leading this conference.

189
13:04.430 --> 13:07.224
‎He gets to perform surgery ‎right before his retirement,

190
13:07.808 --> 13:09.727
‎so I think he's excited.

191
13:29.079 --> 13:29.913
‎Everyone, rise.

192
13:29.997 --> 13:31.165
‎THE 7TH MEDICAL STAFF CONFERENCE

193
13:40.841 --> 13:41.842
‎Please be seated.

194
13:45.971 --> 13:47.973
‎We will now begin the conference.

195
13:48.057 --> 13:51.268
‎The patient is an 80-year-old male, ‎Seo Byeong-gyu.

196
13:51.352 --> 13:54.813
‎He's scheduled for an open cholecystectomy ‎due to suspected gallbladder cancer.

197
13:54.897 --> 13:57.107
‎Per the patient's strong request,

198
13:57.191 --> 13:59.985
‎Director Kim Myeong-seop ‎will personally perform the surgery.

199
14:00.819 --> 14:03.238
‎The surgical technique ‎is the MS Technique,

200
14:03.322 --> 14:05.449
‎which was developed by Director Kim.

201
14:05.532 --> 14:08.243
‎This is a chance to see ‎a legendary yet fundamental technique

202
14:08.327 --> 14:10.746
‎refined over the course of 30 years.

203
14:12.623 --> 14:15.042
‎"MS Technique"? It's just a laparotomy.

204
14:20.005 --> 14:23.258
‎This will be my last chance ‎to reflect on being a surgeon.

205
14:23.342 --> 14:25.469
‎Don't say that, sir.

206
14:27.221 --> 14:28.555
‎As always,

207
14:29.098 --> 14:31.809
‎I'll do my best for the patient.

208
14:31.892 --> 14:35.896
‎Please allow Dr. Bae Heung-gon ‎and Dr. Ma Seong-gyu to assist you.

209
14:36.522 --> 14:38.148
‎I look forward to learning from you.

210
14:39.233 --> 14:41.026
‎Aside from these two,

211
14:41.110 --> 14:43.862
‎I'd like anyone else who is free ‎to observe as well.

212
14:44.488 --> 14:46.031
‎-Thank you. ‎-Thank you.

213
14:49.493 --> 14:50.327
‎Objection.

214
15:03.382 --> 15:04.299
‎Who's that?

215
15:04.800 --> 15:08.679
‎Is that the temporary worker ‎sent by the locum tenens agency?

216
15:08.762 --> 15:10.848
‎Their absolute ace?

217
15:10.931 --> 15:12.599
‎Temporary worker? Ace?

218
15:13.267 --> 15:14.184
‎What do you mean?

219
15:19.982 --> 15:22.317
‎Good. Our intern knows a thing or two.

220
15:22.401 --> 15:23.902
‎Absolute ace, my foot.

221
15:23.986 --> 15:25.696
‎"X" is more like it.

222
15:37.499 --> 15:38.709
‎Do we really need to

223
15:39.626 --> 15:40.544
‎open him up?

224
15:41.336 --> 15:42.838
‎Why open surgery?

225
15:43.464 --> 15:45.883
‎Laparoscopic cholecystectomy ‎has long been the standard

226
15:45.966 --> 15:48.260
‎for quick recovery and stable outcomes.

227
15:48.844 --> 15:51.013
‎Open surgery demands ‎at least a ten-day hospital stay

228
15:51.096 --> 15:52.639
‎and takes a huge toll on the patient.

229
15:53.348 --> 15:54.933
‎So why do you insist on doing it?

230
15:57.102 --> 15:58.562
‎I'm sorry, Director Kim.

231
15:58.645 --> 16:01.356
‎She's the locum who just came…

232
16:03.484 --> 16:05.861
‎You rely on machines a lot, right?

233
16:05.944 --> 16:07.321
‎That's good too.

234
16:07.905 --> 16:09.448
‎Dr. Bae here knows it better than anyone

235
16:09.531 --> 16:12.284
‎since he is renowned ‎as a specialist in laparoscopy.

236
16:12.868 --> 16:15.496
‎This patient is a very fortunate case,

237
16:15.579 --> 16:17.581
‎as his condition was caught ‎on a routine ultrasound

238
16:17.664 --> 16:19.583
‎before any symptoms developed.

239
16:19.666 --> 16:22.336
‎But it's not easy to distinguish

240
16:22.419 --> 16:25.923
‎between inflammation ‎and gallbladder cancer on imaging.

241
16:26.715 --> 16:30.385
‎Given the risk of tumor metastasis,

242
16:30.469 --> 16:33.514
‎any suspicion of gallbladder cancer ‎warrants open surgery.

243
16:33.597 --> 16:36.058
‎Rather than insisting on ‎a minimally invasive approach,

244
16:36.141 --> 16:38.644
‎a case like this requires open surgery.

245
16:38.727 --> 16:40.270
‎Don't you agree, Dr. Bae?

246
16:40.354 --> 16:41.188
‎Yes, sir.

247
16:41.772 --> 16:45.776
‎A lap chole has several disadvantages ‎compared to open surgery

248
16:45.859 --> 16:47.861
‎for early-stage gallbladder cancer--

249
16:47.945 --> 16:50.030
‎Given that this is a very fortunate case

250
16:50.739 --> 16:52.366
‎caught before any symptoms developed,

251
16:52.866 --> 16:55.285
‎early detection of gallbladder cancer ‎means high survival rates,

252
16:55.369 --> 16:58.330
‎so we should choose a surgery ‎that prioritizes the patient's condition.

253
16:59.540 --> 17:01.166
‎He's an 80-year-old elderly man.

254
17:01.250 --> 17:03.544
‎He also developed ‎post-COVID pneumonia three years ago.

255
17:04.086 --> 17:05.796
‎Remove it laparoscopically ‎and do a biopsy.

256
17:05.879 --> 17:06.839
‎Depending on the results,

257
17:06.922 --> 17:09.216
‎we can perform open surgery ‎as a next step.

258
17:09.842 --> 17:10.884
‎She knows her stuff.

259
17:11.385 --> 17:13.137
‎A real surgeon must be able to

260
17:13.220 --> 17:15.806
‎directly visualize ‎and palpate the surgical site

261
17:15.889 --> 17:18.976
‎to handle any bleeding or adhesions.

262
17:19.059 --> 17:21.562
‎They must excise ‎the source of the patient's condition

263
17:21.645 --> 17:25.482
‎as deeply and widely as possible ‎to ensure their safety.

264
17:25.566 --> 17:28.694
‎This is the best way

265
17:28.777 --> 17:29.987
‎to save a patient's life!

266
17:30.070 --> 17:32.114
‎-You're absolutely right, sir! ‎-Yes, you are.

267
17:39.746 --> 17:40.581
‎It seems like…

268
17:42.207 --> 17:45.377
‎you're just excited to get a booking ‎after a million years.

269
17:45.460 --> 17:46.753
‎What? "Get a booking"?

270
17:47.963 --> 17:50.382
‎Where's your sense of respect ‎for the director?

271
17:51.091 --> 17:53.927
‎Then instead of "get a booking," ‎how about…

272
17:56.555 --> 17:57.389
‎Get a reservation?

273
17:58.348 --> 17:59.683
‎"Reservation"?

274
17:59.766 --> 18:02.144
‎How dare you say the director ‎"got a reservation"?

275
18:03.061 --> 18:04.688
‎Just be honest.

276
18:04.771 --> 18:06.815
‎You're eager to take on the case ‎after a long break,

277
18:06.899 --> 18:09.318
‎but you don't know ‎how to do a laparoscopy.

278
18:09.401 --> 18:11.403
‎So you're just stringing together

279
18:11.486 --> 18:13.697
‎a bunch of outdated theories ‎to cover that up.

280
18:14.740 --> 18:17.409
‎If these people in white coats

281
18:17.492 --> 18:19.703
‎actually have medical licenses,

282
18:20.746 --> 18:23.957
‎they'll agree the laparoscopic specialist ‎over there should do it.

283
18:24.499 --> 18:27.169
‎I bet that specialist ‎is thinking the same thing.

284
18:27.252 --> 18:28.795
‎Me? That's not true!

285
18:29.504 --> 18:31.882
‎That's not what I think at all, sir.

286
18:31.965 --> 18:34.760
‎What kind of nonsense are you saying?

287
18:37.221 --> 18:38.055
‎Well…

288
18:40.933 --> 18:42.935
‎You're big on showing proper respect…

289
18:44.394 --> 18:45.229
‎I know.

290
18:45.979 --> 18:47.189
‎This seems appropriate.

291
18:50.275 --> 18:52.694
‎You show excessive greed in your old age.

292
18:55.197 --> 18:56.365
‎Get out!

293
18:56.448 --> 18:58.033
‎What are you doing? Get her out!

294
18:58.992 --> 18:59.826
‎You…

295
19:00.661 --> 19:01.662
‎I'm sorry, Director.

296
19:02.913 --> 19:05.249
‎Please sit down, sir.

297
19:05.332 --> 19:07.209
‎Yes, please take a seat.

298
19:07.292 --> 19:08.627
‎Goodness.

299
19:10.921 --> 19:11.880
‎She's so cool.

300
19:13.757 --> 19:14.925
‎Ms. Jang.

301
19:15.008 --> 19:16.843
‎About that mad dog you sent over…

302
19:16.927 --> 19:18.136
‎I mean, that mad doc…

303
19:18.637 --> 19:21.431
‎I mean, that crazy Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

304
19:22.516 --> 19:23.517
‎What's wrong with her?

305
19:24.851 --> 19:26.478
‎Goodness, is that so?

306
19:27.020 --> 19:30.065
‎It seems Dr. Gye behaved inappropriately.

307
19:30.148 --> 19:31.733
‎DIRECTOR JANG'S LOCUM TENENS AGENCY

308
19:32.651 --> 19:33.652
‎I'm sorry about that.

309
19:34.319 --> 19:36.655
‎Dr. Gye has quite a mouth on her.

310
19:37.322 --> 19:38.865
‎SU-JEONG, FEB. 9: FIRST DAY AT GUMC

311
19:38.949 --> 19:40.450
‎But her skills are undeniable,

312
19:40.951 --> 19:42.828
‎so she'll be a great asset ‎to the hospital.

313
19:43.453 --> 19:45.122
‎I'll take this into consideration

314
19:45.205 --> 19:47.332
‎and charge less for the first month.

315
19:48.041 --> 19:50.669
‎Of course, I'll make sure ‎she gets her act together.

316
19:51.461 --> 19:52.296
‎Yes.

317
19:53.088 --> 19:55.007
‎Thank you. Goodbye.

318
19:57.551 --> 19:59.177
‎-Is it my turn? ‎-Did she get into trouble?

319
19:59.678 --> 20:01.179
‎She just said her piece.

320
20:01.263 --> 20:02.097
‎Here we go.

321
20:04.725 --> 20:06.226
‎I need shoulder acupuncture before you go.

322
20:06.310 --> 20:08.979
‎-Will you pay me in advance? ‎-I'll even cook for you.

323
20:09.479 --> 20:10.814
‎You'll cook for me?

324
20:10.897 --> 20:12.858
‎-Wow, you sure? ‎-One, two, three, four, five.

325
20:17.863 --> 20:19.072
‎Landed on Seoul.

326
20:20.490 --> 20:22.284
‎No, not Seoul…

327
20:24.661 --> 20:27.039
‎When I heard ‎it could be gallbladder cancer,

328
20:27.831 --> 20:29.249
‎my mind went blank.

329
20:30.042 --> 20:35.047
‎Then I remembered seeing you on TV ‎a long time ago.

330
20:35.130 --> 20:36.631
‎After watching the show,

331
20:36.715 --> 20:40.344
‎I realized that gallbladder cancer ‎was very dangerous.

332
20:41.094 --> 20:42.262
‎Yes, well…

333
20:42.346 --> 20:44.890
‎The DBS medical documentary ‎Secrets of Life and Death‎ introduced

334
20:44.973 --> 20:47.017
‎Dr. Kim Myeong-Seop here ‎as the god of gallbladder cancer.

335
20:47.100 --> 20:48.602
‎It's such an honor for us.

336
20:48.685 --> 20:50.729
‎Actually, I've supplied surgical gloves

337
20:50.812 --> 20:54.066
‎to this hospital for over 20 years.

338
20:54.691 --> 20:57.611
‎I supply other hospitals as well,

339
20:57.694 --> 20:59.946
‎but I take great pride in this place--

340
21:00.781 --> 21:03.408
‎-Right, please sign here. ‎-Okay.

341
21:03.492 --> 21:06.912
‎-Director Kim has another appointment. ‎-Oh, I'm sorry.

342
21:06.995 --> 21:08.288
‎By the way…

343
21:10.290 --> 21:12.793
‎It's nothing much, ‎but this is for you.

344
21:14.753 --> 21:17.381
‎I'll get in big trouble if I accept this.

345
21:19.132 --> 21:20.842
‎No, please take it.

346
21:20.926 --> 21:23.845
‎It'll make us feel better if you do.

347
21:23.929 --> 21:25.305
‎We insist.

348
21:25.389 --> 21:27.307
‎-Please take it, Director. ‎-Goodness.

349
21:30.394 --> 21:31.228
‎Thank you.

350
21:34.147 --> 21:35.774
‎Sir, the update is almost done.

351
21:35.857 --> 21:37.901
‎Do you need anything else?

352
21:37.984 --> 21:39.277
‎I'm fine.

353
21:39.361 --> 21:42.155
‎-You can leave after it's done. ‎-Yes, sir.

354
21:53.250 --> 21:54.292
‎Good grief.

355
22:00.590 --> 22:01.758
‎It's all updated, sir.

356
22:02.509 --> 22:03.343
‎Get rid of this.

357
22:04.177 --> 22:06.430
‎-And empty the trash. ‎-Yes. Thank you, sir.

358
22:17.399 --> 22:18.358
‎"Thank you, sir"?

359
22:18.984 --> 22:20.360
‎Why did I thank him?

360
22:22.362 --> 22:23.488
‎What's that?

361
22:23.572 --> 22:24.531
‎It's ‎jocheong‎.

362
22:25.323 --> 22:27.576
‎Jocheong‎? Like that rich honey?

363
22:29.077 --> 22:31.538
‎It's homemade. ‎The store-bought kind isn't this color.

364
22:31.621 --> 22:32.831
‎How do you know that?

365
22:33.832 --> 22:36.501
‎My grandmother always made me some ‎for the holidays.

366
22:37.294 --> 22:40.088
‎And she made some for good luck ‎when I took the college entrance exam.

367
22:40.172 --> 22:42.549
‎She was going to make some ‎for my medical licensing exam,

368
22:43.133 --> 22:44.593
‎but she passed away two years ago.

369
22:45.177 --> 22:46.678
‎Then you can have it.

370
22:47.304 --> 22:49.723
‎You have to stir the pot all night ‎just to make this much.

371
22:49.806 --> 22:51.349
‎At least try a spoonful.

372
22:52.017 --> 22:53.435
‎She must've worked so hard.

373
22:54.227 --> 22:56.438
‎I'm sure she made it ‎with genuine gratitude.

374
22:56.521 --> 22:58.356
‎You're the sentimental type, aren't you?

375
22:58.440 --> 22:59.691
‎What?

376
23:00.275 --> 23:02.194
‎Never mind. Take good care of them.

377
23:03.820 --> 23:04.696
‎Yes, sir.

378
23:07.782 --> 23:09.951
‎RESUME

379
23:10.952 --> 23:12.829
‎Let's just fire her right now.

380
23:12.913 --> 23:14.789
‎She's so damn disrespectful.

381
23:18.001 --> 23:21.213
‎I got the signed consent form ‎and updated the director's computer.

382
23:21.296 --> 23:22.297
‎Good work.

383
23:23.840 --> 23:25.592
‎Come on, Dr. Do.

384
23:25.675 --> 23:26.509
‎Hey.

385
23:27.260 --> 23:28.094
‎Read this.

386
23:31.264 --> 23:32.599
‎"Gye Su-jeong."

387
23:32.682 --> 23:34.976
‎Her name is Gye Su-jeong?

388
23:35.060 --> 23:37.145
‎Man, she's older than I thought.

389
23:37.771 --> 23:39.314
‎Medical school at Cubanacan University

390
23:39.856 --> 23:41.107
‎and the University of Florida.

391
23:41.775 --> 23:43.026
‎Below that.

392
23:44.569 --> 23:48.031
‎"Returned to Korea after volunteering ‎in remote medical missions worldwide."

393
23:48.698 --> 23:50.700
‎"General surgery. Cardiothoracic surgery."

394
23:50.784 --> 23:52.661
‎She's got some skills for her age.

395
23:53.245 --> 23:54.246
‎That's so cool.

396
23:54.996 --> 23:55.956
‎Hey.

397
23:56.039 --> 23:58.875
‎Dr. Bae is double-board certified ‎in neurosurgery and general.

398
24:00.418 --> 24:04.673
‎"Registered as a surgical locum ‎at the Jang Hui-suk Locum Tenens Agency."

399
24:05.257 --> 24:06.466
‎"Hobbies, surgery."

400
24:06.549 --> 24:08.260
‎"Special skills, surgery."

401
24:08.343 --> 24:09.970
‎It's all surgery.

402
24:10.553 --> 24:11.805
‎Seems like a scam artist.

403
24:11.888 --> 24:13.932
‎-We're keeping her on? ‎-Look into her, sir.

404
24:14.015 --> 24:16.309
‎Why would she come here with this resume?

405
24:17.769 --> 24:20.605
‎What do you mean? ‎What's wrong with our hospital?

406
24:20.689 --> 24:23.108
‎That's not what I meant, sir.

407
24:27.612 --> 24:28.655
‎Hey. You…

408
24:32.325 --> 24:35.954
‎For now, you'll assist Dr. Ma Seong-gyu ‎and Dr. Park Tae-gyeong.

409
24:43.378 --> 24:44.296
‎Please.

410
24:45.630 --> 24:46.631
‎Assist them with what?

411
24:46.715 --> 24:47.632
‎What else?

412
24:47.716 --> 24:49.843
‎Just follow these two around.

413
24:49.926 --> 24:51.219
‎Let's prep for the conference.

414
24:51.720 --> 24:53.054
‎Get going.

415
25:00.770 --> 25:01.646
‎Now what?

416
25:01.730 --> 25:04.983
‎We're short on staff, ‎so we'll try her out for a week.

417
25:05.817 --> 25:06.776
‎It's free.

418
25:07.610 --> 25:09.821
‎Keep her glued to her desk ‎and away from Director Kim.

419
25:19.414 --> 25:21.833
‎SEO BYEONG-GYU, M/80 ‎OPERATES A RUBBER FACTORY

420
25:30.717 --> 25:31.634
‎Excuse me.

421
25:34.054 --> 25:35.180
‎The inguinal hernia…

422
25:37.223 --> 25:39.476
‎Do you remember me from the pool hall?

423
25:40.852 --> 25:42.812
‎Your diagnosis was spot on,

424
25:42.896 --> 25:44.606
‎and he went straight into surgery.

425
25:46.107 --> 25:46.983
‎By the way…

426
25:48.109 --> 25:49.402
‎what does this mean?

427
25:49.486 --> 25:51.196
‎When do people draw an "X"?

428
25:53.031 --> 25:54.324
‎Well, I guess to say…

429
25:54.824 --> 25:56.326
‎"That's not it" or "That won't do"?

430
25:56.409 --> 25:57.786
‎There you go.

431
26:00.872 --> 26:01.915
‎"You're…

432
26:02.415 --> 26:03.249
‎not it."

433
26:03.750 --> 26:05.710
‎"You're not good enough"?

434
26:06.586 --> 26:08.546
‎You don't think I'm good enough?

435
26:08.630 --> 26:10.799
‎Why not? Why do I get an "X"?

436
26:10.882 --> 26:13.593
‎I never told you to look at ‎Mr. Seo Byeong-gyu's chart.

437
26:13.676 --> 26:15.136
‎He runs a rubber factory.

438
26:15.220 --> 26:18.264
‎Yes, and he also supplies ‎surgical gloves here.

439
26:18.348 --> 26:21.142
‎-He seemed very proud of it. ‎-Just do the work I gave you.

440
26:21.226 --> 26:23.478
‎Would you want Director Kim ‎to operate on you?

441
26:23.561 --> 26:24.396
‎What?

442
26:24.479 --> 26:27.023
‎You're a doctor, ‎so you know this is unnecessary.

443
26:27.107 --> 26:29.651
‎That was all settled at the conference.

444
26:29.734 --> 26:30.944
‎Would you want him to?

445
26:32.445 --> 26:33.947
‎-Of course. ‎-Then…

446
26:36.574 --> 26:37.492
‎what about your parents?

447
26:38.785 --> 26:40.954
‎Not you, but your mother.

448
26:42.872 --> 26:44.207
‎That's an extreme scenario--

449
26:44.290 --> 26:46.042
‎This patient has a child too.

450
26:47.252 --> 26:48.253
‎They're just not a doctor.

451
26:51.047 --> 26:52.173
‎I'd want him to.

452
26:52.715 --> 26:56.803
‎I'd want Director Kim ‎to operate on my mother for me.

453
26:57.762 --> 26:59.973
‎And if I were that patient's child,

454
27:00.682 --> 27:03.768
‎he'd most definitely have ‎Director Kim as his surgeon

455
27:03.852 --> 27:05.228
‎for the sake of my future.

456
27:07.355 --> 27:10.525
‎I need you to revise this ‎and send it back to me.

457
27:10.608 --> 27:12.444
‎-Yes, sir. ‎-Good.

458
27:13.486 --> 27:16.531
‎-What's going on? ‎-I'm so glad you're here, Dr. Bae.

459
27:17.866 --> 27:20.452
‎This is why I don't like you people.

460
27:21.244 --> 27:23.288
‎What did she just say?

461
27:23.371 --> 27:25.081
‎"You people"?

462
27:25.165 --> 27:29.294
‎-No, sir. You misheard her. ‎-He heard me right.

463
27:29.878 --> 27:31.212
‎-Hey. ‎-I said…

464
27:32.881 --> 27:33.923
‎I don't like you people.

465
27:36.426 --> 27:39.012
‎People who only studied ‎to get rich and climb the ladder.

466
27:39.971 --> 27:41.389
‎People with no ethics, no beliefs,

467
27:41.473 --> 27:44.100
‎and no independent thought, ‎who are smart yet stupid.

468
27:44.184 --> 27:45.393
‎You grovel to superiors

469
27:45.477 --> 27:46.895
‎while lording it over patients.

470
27:46.978 --> 27:50.190
‎You suck up to superiors and bully nurses.

471
27:50.273 --> 27:53.526
‎You ignore corruption at the top ‎and blame the system for your own mess.

472
27:53.610 --> 27:57.238
‎You irresponsible people ‎care only for your own comfort,

473
27:57.322 --> 27:58.615
‎so you leave surgery to an old man

474
27:58.698 --> 28:02.285
‎who neglects his health and skills ‎and is lucky if his hands don't shake.

475
28:02.368 --> 28:04.037
‎You're really pushing it.

476
28:04.120 --> 28:06.998
‎You know full well ‎how much the patient will suffer

477
28:07.081 --> 28:08.500
‎with his life on the line,

478
28:09.417 --> 28:12.754
‎yet you only think about ‎how to get off the hook,

479
28:12.837 --> 28:13.838
‎complacent as ever.

480
28:13.922 --> 28:15.757
‎You expect patients

481
28:15.840 --> 28:18.551
‎who are much older than you ‎to bow at the waist and say,

482
28:18.635 --> 28:20.887
‎"Please save me" and "Thank you."

483
28:22.013 --> 28:23.139
‎You people…

484
28:23.806 --> 28:25.683
‎are merely doctors by name.

485
28:26.559 --> 28:27.393
‎Wow.

486
28:29.812 --> 28:30.980
‎You are the worst.

487
28:32.565 --> 28:33.942
‎Have you lost your mind?

488
28:34.025 --> 28:35.693
‎-Get out. ‎-Get out.

489
28:36.277 --> 28:37.654
‎-Get the hell out. ‎-Out!

490
28:38.488 --> 28:41.032
‎What are you looking at? Want to fight?

491
28:42.158 --> 28:44.494
‎Come on. Let's see what you've got.

492
28:44.577 --> 28:45.954
‎Come at me. I dare you.

493
28:47.580 --> 28:50.124
‎What's that for? ‎Are you going to hit me with it?

494
28:51.334 --> 28:52.168
‎Six o'clock!

495
28:56.172 --> 28:57.340
‎That's right.

496
28:57.423 --> 28:59.050
‎-Just leave. ‎-Oh.

497
29:00.552 --> 29:01.594
‎"Oh"?

498
29:05.723 --> 29:07.225
‎What? Don't tell me…

499
29:09.769 --> 29:10.645
‎She clocked out?

500
29:12.272 --> 29:14.148
‎Go and bring her back.

501
29:14.232 --> 29:15.441
‎-Yes, sir. ‎-Right now.

502
29:16.359 --> 29:18.736
‎How dare she clock out?

503
29:48.224 --> 29:49.934
‎SEO ******-GYU

504
30:01.446 --> 30:02.363
‎I knew it.

505
30:02.447 --> 30:04.908
‎It was a good idea ‎to have Director Kim operate,

506
30:04.991 --> 30:07.076
‎seeing the doctors ‎taking turns to check up on us.

507
30:07.577 --> 30:09.245
‎-Someone else was here? ‎-Yes.

508
30:09.329 --> 30:10.747
‎They were just here.

509
30:11.706 --> 30:12.540
‎Here.

510
30:13.041 --> 30:14.500
‎Have some mango too.

511
30:15.919 --> 30:18.421
‎Our daughter bought some ‎from the department store

512
30:18.504 --> 30:19.547
‎to cheer up her sick dad,

513
30:20.673 --> 30:22.759
‎since he'll need to fast soon.

514
30:22.842 --> 30:23.801
‎It's very sweet.

515
30:24.469 --> 30:27.263
‎The other doctor really enjoyed it.

516
30:27.805 --> 30:30.516
‎You gave them some yogurt too, right?

517
30:30.600 --> 30:31.768
‎Of course.

518
30:33.061 --> 30:36.105
‎By the way, they're a doctor, right?

519
30:36.606 --> 30:38.024
‎Did you catch their name?

520
30:38.107 --> 30:39.943
‎They weren't wearing a white coat,

521
30:40.485 --> 30:41.653
‎but said they were a doctor.

522
30:42.695 --> 30:44.614
‎-Was it a woman? ‎-Yes.

523
30:45.823 --> 30:48.534
‎She did say something odd.

524
30:49.786 --> 30:52.372
‎She suggested pushing back the surgery.

525
30:53.539 --> 30:56.042
‎Everything is okay ‎with Director Kim, right?

526
30:56.125 --> 30:58.836
‎Of course. Did she say anything else?

527
30:58.920 --> 31:02.215
‎When I told her ‎I couldn't postpone because of my factory,

528
31:02.298 --> 31:05.635
‎she asked if I'd like a different surgeon.

529
31:05.718 --> 31:07.387
‎I told her absolutely not

530
31:07.470 --> 31:10.264
‎and insisted on getting surgery ‎from the director.

531
31:11.849 --> 31:13.518
‎She was probably just asking.

532
31:14.727 --> 31:17.897
‎I'm sure tomorrow's surgery will go well.

533
31:17.981 --> 31:19.107
‎Oh, yes.

534
31:19.190 --> 31:20.108
‎Thank you.

535
31:20.191 --> 31:21.317
‎Thank you for this.

536
31:21.401 --> 31:22.652
‎-Of course. ‎-Get some rest.

537
32:03.067 --> 32:04.861
‎-Try this first. ‎-Still,

538
32:05.528 --> 32:07.822
‎it's the largest hub hospital ‎in the suburbs of Seoul.

539
32:08.406 --> 32:10.033
‎But there's less meddling than in Seoul,

540
32:10.116 --> 32:13.077
‎so they're shadier, ‎leaving us with lots of ways to profit.

541
32:13.161 --> 32:14.037
‎It's good for us.

542
32:14.787 --> 32:16.581
‎-Good for you, you mean. ‎-What?

543
32:18.207 --> 32:19.042
‎Su-jeong.

544
32:19.125 --> 32:21.044
‎Breathe. Don't inhale your food.

545
32:22.462 --> 32:24.922
‎Take shorter showers. ‎The gas bill went up.

546
32:25.757 --> 32:27.091
‎But I pay my bills.

547
32:30.136 --> 32:30.970
‎That director…

548
32:31.554 --> 32:32.597
‎Who? Kim Myeong-seop?

549
32:32.680 --> 32:34.057
‎You know anything about him?

550
32:35.558 --> 32:37.894
‎Can't tell you for free. ‎I'll dock your pay.

551
32:38.478 --> 32:41.022
‎Jeez, you're savage.

552
32:41.105 --> 32:42.190
‎Here, eat up.

553
32:44.984 --> 32:46.027
‎Gosh, who cooked this?

554
32:48.154 --> 32:51.074
‎I should've come sooner, Director Kim.

555
32:51.157 --> 32:52.450
‎Skip the pleasantries.

556
32:53.034 --> 32:56.162
‎We normally only give this ‎after signing a contract,

557
32:56.245 --> 32:59.207
‎but please accept this with our apologies.

558
33:00.708 --> 33:04.962
‎Is this the famous melon gift ‎that represents your agency?

559
33:05.046 --> 33:07.715
‎I appreciate you recognizing it.

560
33:09.342 --> 33:11.761
‎-I left the contents with the secretary. ‎-You did?

561
33:15.181 --> 33:17.308
‎You know you have to keep the box, right?

562
33:17.391 --> 33:18.267
‎Oh, right.

563
33:23.147 --> 33:25.274
‎The melon looks delicious.

564
33:26.400 --> 33:28.569
‎This is a top-grade melon.

565
33:29.195 --> 33:30.947
‎It's from overseas and hard to get.

566
33:31.030 --> 33:31.906
‎Really?

567
33:33.449 --> 33:36.744
‎Dr. Gye lived overseas for a long time,

568
33:37.328 --> 33:39.497
‎so she's not familiar ‎with Korean medical culture.

569
33:39.580 --> 33:43.459
‎She wasn't aware of ‎your outstanding legacy,

570
33:43.543 --> 33:44.710
‎so please forgive her.

571
33:45.711 --> 33:46.546
‎All right.

572
33:46.629 --> 33:48.339
‎Dr. Gye has many shortcomings.

573
33:49.215 --> 33:52.385
‎Just give her some scut work ‎and keep her around.

574
33:52.468 --> 33:54.095
‎She just doesn't know any better.

575
33:56.013 --> 33:58.474
‎I'd like to observe your surgery, sir.

576
33:58.558 --> 34:00.268
‎Oh, really?

577
34:00.351 --> 34:02.854
‎Yes. I'd like to see you f…

578
34:02.937 --> 34:04.689
‎I mean, see you demonstrate ‎the MS Technique.

579
34:05.523 --> 34:06.524
‎All right.

580
34:07.191 --> 34:08.025
‎You can observe.

581
34:08.985 --> 34:09.819
‎Thank you.

582
34:17.743 --> 34:19.912
‎He hasn't performed surgery in a while,

583
34:20.621 --> 34:22.248
‎and all eyes will be on him.

584
34:22.331 --> 34:23.291
‎I'll cover for him.

585
34:23.374 --> 34:25.459
‎Without him knowing, got it?

586
34:25.543 --> 34:27.086
‎Yes, of course.

587
34:30.214 --> 34:31.507
‎Where's Dr. Gye?

588
34:32.383 --> 34:34.802
‎Why ask that before surgery and jinx it?

589
34:34.886 --> 34:37.013
‎I didn't know that would jinx it.

590
34:37.722 --> 34:38.931
‎You always get the last word.

591
34:39.015 --> 34:41.767
‎I'll let you have the last word next time.

592
34:41.851 --> 34:43.019
‎You little punk.

593
34:49.734 --> 34:51.611
‎Dr. Bu, you made it.

594
34:51.694 --> 34:53.863
‎Director Kim said he invited you.

595
34:53.946 --> 34:55.239
‎It's been a while.

596
34:55.323 --> 34:56.949
‎It's so nice to see you here.

597
34:57.450 --> 34:59.118
‎How do you like it over there?

598
35:00.828 --> 35:02.955
‎I'm just doing my best.

599
35:11.130 --> 35:12.048
‎You're here.

600
35:18.054 --> 35:18.971
‎Goodness.

601
35:19.555 --> 35:23.309
‎Dr. Bu came to watch ‎Director Kim and his miracle hands, huh?

602
35:24.477 --> 35:27.521
‎He was in line to become director ‎at the main hospital,

603
35:27.605 --> 35:29.148
‎but he got pushed out

604
35:29.232 --> 35:32.068
‎and is now working at the southern branch.

605
35:32.151 --> 35:34.904
‎Oh my, I see.

606
35:36.030 --> 35:37.740
‎But why did he get pushed out?

607
35:38.324 --> 35:39.617
‎He's no fun to be around,

608
35:40.159 --> 35:42.370
‎and he's the very model ‎of a devoted doctor.

609
35:42.453 --> 35:44.705
‎It's no wonder ‎other doctors can't stand him.

610
35:46.457 --> 35:48.209
‎I see.

611
35:49.043 --> 35:51.462
‎He's no fun in more ways than one.

612
36:16.320 --> 36:18.698
‎No, bring me powdered gloves.

613
36:19.407 --> 36:21.367
‎-Excuse me? ‎-These make my hands sweaty.

614
36:21.450 --> 36:22.994
‎We have some ready, sir.

615
36:24.787 --> 36:25.788
‎Right.

616
36:34.964 --> 36:37.133
‎The induction was uneventful,

617
36:37.216 --> 36:38.509
‎and his vitals are stable.

618
36:52.273 --> 36:55.192
‎We're finally recording ‎this legendary surgery.

619
36:55.276 --> 36:57.445
‎I never knew that CCTV ‎had a purpose until today.

620
36:57.528 --> 36:59.447
‎No need to be nervous.

621
36:59.530 --> 37:00.823
‎I'll do what I always do.

622
37:10.875 --> 37:12.251
‎Very nice, Dr. Bae.

623
37:12.335 --> 37:14.128
‎I used to listen to this

624
37:14.211 --> 37:18.007
‎and remove two gallbladders at once ‎using my technique.

625
37:18.090 --> 37:18.924
‎Turn up the volume.

626
37:21.260 --> 37:22.970
‎I can't hear the monitor.

627
37:23.929 --> 37:24.764
‎Turn it down.

628
37:25.556 --> 37:26.932
‎Let's begin.

629
37:27.516 --> 37:29.685
‎Director Kim Myeong-seop's cholecystectomy

630
37:29.769 --> 37:31.395
‎for Mr. Seo Byeong-gyu will now begin.

631
37:31.479 --> 37:32.813
‎-Let's do a good job. ‎-Let's do a good job.

632
37:42.656 --> 37:43.491
‎Scalpel.

633
37:48.954 --> 37:51.499
‎I warned them ‎not to offer the scalpel first.

634
37:51.582 --> 37:54.752
‎Doesn't it make things easier ‎when they take the initiative?

635
37:54.835 --> 37:57.046
‎It's his way of saying,

636
37:57.129 --> 37:59.382
‎"You're just a nurse. How dare you?"

637
38:00.174 --> 38:02.051
‎He made a lot of nurses cry.

638
38:02.134 --> 38:03.636
‎What an ass.

639
38:03.719 --> 38:04.637
‎An asset.

640
38:05.638 --> 38:07.056
‎He's a good asset.

641
38:12.770 --> 38:15.606
‎You should stop the surgery ‎and take him in for an MRI.

642
38:16.607 --> 38:18.401
‎Why do an MRI for the patient?

643
38:18.901 --> 38:20.486
‎Not the patient. Director Kim.

644
38:21.070 --> 38:23.030
‎What kind of nonsense is that?

645
38:23.739 --> 38:24.824
‎Want to get kicked out?

646
38:24.907 --> 38:27.743
‎Oh my, Dr. Gye is talking crap again.

647
38:27.827 --> 38:29.328
‎Come over here, Dr. Gye.

648
38:32.289 --> 38:33.207
‎Be quiet.

649
38:33.791 --> 38:35.000
‎This should be fun.

650
38:45.803 --> 38:47.221
‎Who turned the volume down?

651
38:54.228 --> 38:55.104
‎Hurry up. Sponge.

652
38:59.692 --> 39:00.568
‎MS forceps.

653
39:03.571 --> 39:05.865
‎These custom forceps were designed

654
39:05.948 --> 39:07.616
‎for the technique named after me.

655
39:07.700 --> 39:10.161
‎I used to do at least ‎four surgeries a day with these.

656
39:10.244 --> 39:11.245
‎That's amazing, sir.

657
39:12.997 --> 39:15.708
‎I'll give these to you after this surgery.

658
39:15.791 --> 39:17.293
‎I'd be honored, sir.

659
39:19.837 --> 39:21.714
‎Experienced surgeons normally do

660
39:21.797 --> 39:23.090
‎ten cases a day.

661
39:23.799 --> 39:24.967
‎He's slow as hell.

662
39:31.807 --> 39:32.808
‎Wipe.

663
39:38.314 --> 39:39.148
‎Look at this.

664
39:39.231 --> 39:41.650
‎Recurrent inflammation ‎has caused severe adhesions.

665
39:42.401 --> 39:44.487
‎Opening him up was the right call.

666
40:14.558 --> 40:15.559
‎MS forceps.

667
40:19.313 --> 40:21.857
‎Look at how elegantly it grabs hold.

668
40:22.358 --> 40:23.567
‎Right angle.

669
40:29.323 --> 40:31.158
‎What are you doing? ‎There's sweat in my eyes.

670
40:34.828 --> 40:35.913
‎Right angle.

671
40:36.956 --> 40:37.957
‎Metz.

672
40:43.045 --> 40:45.631
‎BP dropping. Systolic's under 60. ‎Heart rate's over 150.

673
40:45.714 --> 40:46.632
‎Vitals are unstable.

674
40:53.764 --> 40:55.099
‎Patient's in shock. Pushing a bolus.

675
40:56.725 --> 40:58.102
‎-Director Kim? ‎-Director, how…

676
40:58.686 --> 40:59.520
‎Sir?

677
40:59.603 --> 41:01.063
‎You need to raise your mask.

678
41:03.065 --> 41:04.608
‎-Sir? ‎-Director Kim?

679
41:04.692 --> 41:06.569
‎-Director? ‎-Your mask, sir.

680
41:06.652 --> 41:07.987
‎Sir, are you okay?

681
41:08.070 --> 41:09.280
‎What's happening?

682
41:09.363 --> 41:11.407
‎Director Kim, wake up.

683
41:11.490 --> 41:13.200
‎Sir, are you with me?

684
41:13.284 --> 41:15.202
‎Squeeze my hand, sir.

685
41:15.286 --> 41:17.079
‎-What's going on? ‎-Mental status is declining.

686
41:17.162 --> 41:18.998
‎It looks like left-sided hemiplegia!

687
41:19.081 --> 41:20.874
‎CVA, likely an ischemic stroke.

688
41:20.958 --> 41:21.959
‎-Run a CT. ‎-Bring a stretcher!

689
41:22.042 --> 41:24.378
‎Vitals are unstable. ‎We risk contamination, so clear out now!

690
41:24.461 --> 41:27.089
‎Secure an IV line ‎and start fluids for Director Kim, now.

691
41:27.172 --> 41:28.507
‎Call neurosurgery!

692
41:28.591 --> 41:30.175
‎Wait, have Dr. Bae stay with him!

693
41:30.259 --> 41:31.135
‎-I'll be right there! ‎-Okay!

694
41:31.218 --> 41:32.386
‎One, two.

695
41:32.469 --> 41:34.346
‎What about this patient? He's in shock!

696
41:34.430 --> 41:35.264
‎Get in here!

697
41:35.347 --> 41:37.016
‎What about this patient?

698
41:37.099 --> 41:39.184
‎Dr. Bae! Dr. Ma!

699
41:39.268 --> 41:41.103
‎-Hurry up. ‎-You can't all leave!

700
41:41.186 --> 41:42.521
‎What about the patient?

701
41:42.605 --> 41:44.148
‎Stay here for now and watch him.

702
41:44.231 --> 41:45.941
‎What? Where are you going, Dr. Bae?

703
41:46.025 --> 41:46.942
‎Ma Seong-gyu!

704
41:47.026 --> 41:47.985
‎Hey!

705
42:11.300 --> 42:13.385
‎Dr. Jo, what do we do?

706
42:13.469 --> 42:15.512
‎I'm keeping his vitals stable. ‎Page someone.

707
42:15.596 --> 42:18.098
‎Everyone who wasn't in surgery

708
42:18.182 --> 42:19.933
‎was here, but they left.

709
42:20.017 --> 42:21.018
‎There's no one to page.

710
42:21.101 --> 42:22.603
‎It doesn't matter. Call anyone.

711
42:29.485 --> 42:30.653
‎Should I try?

712
42:31.153 --> 42:31.987
‎What?

713
42:32.071 --> 42:36.075
‎This patient is alone ‎and fighting for his life.

714
42:37.993 --> 42:39.662
‎I have to try something…

715
42:41.747 --> 42:43.957
‎But there are too many instruments.

716
42:44.541 --> 42:46.669
‎You're an intern, you idiot!

717
42:46.752 --> 42:48.045
‎Call a resident right now!

718
42:48.128 --> 42:50.172
‎But there's no one available…

719
42:54.968 --> 42:55.886
‎There ‎is‎ someone.

720
43:23.622 --> 43:24.623
‎Vitals?

721
43:25.207 --> 43:27.292
‎Can't get a BP. Heart rate is 170.

722
43:29.128 --> 43:30.671
‎All right.

723
43:30.754 --> 43:34.049
‎Everyone, put your hands up.

724
43:36.093 --> 43:37.886
‎I brought what you asked for.

725
43:37.970 --> 43:40.889
‎Everyone switch to those gloves ‎and change into new scrubs.

726
43:40.973 --> 43:42.933
‎Let's max out the room air exchange.

727
43:43.016 --> 43:45.269
‎-Push epi and dex. ‎-Got it.

728
43:47.146 --> 43:48.355
‎You'll assist.

729
43:48.439 --> 43:49.273
‎Okay.

730
44:04.204 --> 44:05.289
‎The alarms stopped.

731
44:10.043 --> 44:10.878
‎Turn off the music.

732
44:13.172 --> 44:14.590
‎BP's 120 over 65.

733
44:14.673 --> 44:15.841
‎Heart rate is 90.

734
44:28.312 --> 44:29.563
‎Resuming surgery.

735
44:30.522 --> 44:31.482
‎Tie 2-0 silk.

736
44:38.197 --> 44:39.031
‎Off.

737
44:41.283 --> 44:42.117
‎Scissors.

738
44:44.203 --> 44:45.037
‎Tie.

739
44:53.837 --> 44:54.671
‎Off.

740
45:07.142 --> 45:08.185
‎Sponge forceps.

741
45:08.810 --> 45:09.811
‎Hold this.

742
45:10.479 --> 45:11.730
‎Forceps.

743
45:30.791 --> 45:31.625
‎Right angle.

744
45:32.960 --> 45:35.921
‎Pass me whatever you think I'll need next. ‎I'll ask if I need something else.

745
45:36.004 --> 45:37.172
‎Yes, Doctor.

746
45:44.513 --> 45:45.639
‎Cystic duct ligation.

747
45:46.265 --> 45:47.599
‎She has quick hands, doesn't she?

748
45:51.436 --> 45:53.689
‎I'm the head of the country's ‎first-ever locum tenens agency.

749
45:53.772 --> 45:54.940
‎My name is Jang Hui-suk.

750
45:55.023 --> 45:56.400
‎DIRECTOR JANG HUI-SUK ‎LOCUM TENENS AGENCY

751
45:56.483 --> 45:58.860
‎And that's our agency's star surgeon,

752
45:58.944 --> 46:00.904
‎Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

753
46:12.374 --> 46:14.251
‎Specimen's out. Send it to pathology.

754
46:15.877 --> 46:16.878
‎Gauze count?

755
46:17.379 --> 46:18.922
‎All gauze accounted for.

756
46:20.632 --> 46:21.717
‎Let's close up.

757
46:24.678 --> 46:26.638
‎OPERATION TIME, TIME, ANESTHESIA TIME

758
46:40.110 --> 46:41.695
‎Estimated blood loss?

759
46:41.778 --> 46:43.739
‎-200 cc. ‎-Before the patient wakes, let's push--

760
46:43.822 --> 46:45.782
‎Pushing 100 mg of hydrocortisone.

761
46:49.578 --> 46:50.621
‎We're finished here.

762
47:37.250 --> 47:38.335
‎Dr. Gye?

763
47:41.546 --> 47:42.589
‎Thank you for your hard work.

764
47:47.177 --> 47:48.095
‎Thank you.

765
47:49.763 --> 47:50.639
‎Thank you!

766
47:51.139 --> 47:52.307
‎Thank you.

767
48:06.196 --> 48:08.740
‎Oh my goodness. You're still here, Dr. Bu?

768
48:09.324 --> 48:11.076
‎I left my phone here.

769
48:11.159 --> 48:12.160
‎I'm all over the place.

770
48:15.038 --> 48:16.748
‎Director Kim pulled through.

771
48:16.832 --> 48:20.043
‎Our neurosurgery team and Dr. Bae ‎did excellent work.

772
48:21.294 --> 48:22.212
‎That's good to hear.

773
48:22.295 --> 48:24.464
‎But that crazy doctor…

774
48:25.132 --> 48:27.426
‎How on earth did she know?

775
48:30.637 --> 48:32.305
‎Have you lost your mind?

776
48:32.389 --> 48:33.849
‎What did you give him?

777
48:33.932 --> 48:35.684
‎Dr. Bae, he's breathing.

778
48:37.269 --> 48:39.187
‎Move fast and restore blood flow.

779
48:50.407 --> 48:52.325
‎DIRECTOR JANG HUI-SUK ‎LOCUM TENENS AGENCY

780
49:38.663 --> 49:39.748
‎Dr. Gye!

781
49:53.845 --> 49:56.681
‎So Dr. Gye performed the surgery?

782
49:57.432 --> 49:58.892
‎Did you page her?

783
49:58.975 --> 50:00.977
‎Are you reprimanding Dr. Park?

784
50:01.520 --> 50:03.104
‎The bigger issue ‎was that no one was there.

785
50:03.188 --> 50:04.689
‎It was an emergency situation,

786
50:04.773 --> 50:07.150
‎and we ended up ‎with another patient on our hands--

787
50:07.234 --> 50:09.361
‎And it mattered more ‎because it was the director, right?

788
50:09.444 --> 50:11.321
‎How could you leave a patient like that?

789
50:11.404 --> 50:13.031
‎So should we have abandoned him?

790
50:13.657 --> 50:15.033
‎Director Kim is a patient too.

791
50:15.116 --> 50:17.577
‎You should've secured ‎a primary surgeon first!

792
50:29.548 --> 50:31.007
‎What are you doing?

793
50:31.091 --> 50:32.425
‎Put that down right now.

794
50:35.136 --> 50:36.429
‎Dr. Gye.

795
50:36.513 --> 50:38.807
‎You performed that surgery ‎without permission.

796
50:42.686 --> 50:46.398
‎You just saw Mr. Seo go into shock ‎from an unknown cause.

797
50:47.065 --> 50:48.567
‎"Unknown cause"?

798
50:50.318 --> 50:51.194
‎You know the cause.

799
50:51.987 --> 50:53.780
‎Come on, admit it.

800
50:53.864 --> 50:54.948
‎Will you answer…

801
50:58.451 --> 51:00.328
‎Stop. Just stop!

802
51:00.412 --> 51:01.413
‎Stop eating!

803
51:07.586 --> 51:08.920
‎Here.

804
51:10.005 --> 51:12.757
‎Here and here. You're all doctors here.

805
51:14.634 --> 51:15.635
‎Look for it.

806
51:15.719 --> 51:16.845
‎That injection.

807
51:16.928 --> 51:18.388
‎It was epinephrine, right?

808
51:18.471 --> 51:20.265
‎EPINEPHRINE: ‎TREATMENT FOR ALLERGIC REACTIONS

809
51:20.348 --> 51:21.433
‎Why won't you answer?

810
51:22.434 --> 51:23.602
‎Me?

811
51:24.394 --> 51:25.395
‎What?

812
51:26.313 --> 51:29.107
‎Why are you staring at me?

813
51:30.775 --> 51:31.860
‎Six o'clock!

814
51:34.112 --> 51:35.947
‎Again?

815
51:37.198 --> 51:38.450
‎A clock was behind me again?

816
51:38.533 --> 51:40.994
‎-Go and catch her. ‎-Yes, sir.

817
51:45.040 --> 51:46.625
‎Epinephrine?

818
51:47.542 --> 51:50.045
‎But Director Kim had an ischemic stroke.

819
51:50.629 --> 51:52.255
‎In the observation gallery,

820
51:52.923 --> 51:54.549
‎Dr. Gye said to do an MRI on him.

821
51:54.633 --> 51:55.592
‎What?

822
51:57.427 --> 52:00.055
‎I think she knew he was going to collapse.

823
52:14.861 --> 52:16.655
‎SEO ******-GYU

824
52:20.367 --> 52:21.576
‎I'm not catching anyone.

825
52:23.036 --> 52:25.246
‎Just go home, Dr. Gye.

826
52:31.044 --> 52:33.254
‎GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

827
52:33.838 --> 52:35.090
‎Dr. Do.

828
52:35.173 --> 52:36.341
‎Yes?

829
52:36.424 --> 52:39.094
‎Did Dr. Gye perform the surgery?

830
52:39.844 --> 52:41.930
‎He's asking if you performed the surgery.

831
52:43.807 --> 52:45.016
‎There you go again.

832
52:45.600 --> 52:46.434
‎Yes?

833
52:46.518 --> 52:47.560
‎Tell her she did a good job.

834
52:47.644 --> 52:50.772
‎As expected, doing a laparotomy ‎with the MS Technique

835
52:51.398 --> 52:52.232
‎was the right move.

836
52:52.315 --> 52:53.274
‎Yes, sir.

837
52:54.567 --> 52:55.777
‎He says, "Good job."

838
52:55.860 --> 52:59.572
‎"As expected, doing a laparotomy ‎with the MS Technique was the right move."

839
52:59.656 --> 53:01.950
‎No. As expected, ‎you shouldn't have opened him up.

840
53:02.659 --> 53:04.828
‎If there's nothing else, please excuse me.

841
53:05.328 --> 53:06.246
‎Dr. Gye.

842
53:09.040 --> 53:10.458
‎Tell her I'm firing her.

843
53:11.459 --> 53:12.377
‎What a nutjob.

844
53:15.755 --> 53:18.425
‎"You're fired, you nutjob,"

845
53:18.508 --> 53:19.342
‎is what he says.

846
53:29.185 --> 53:31.646
‎What's a doctor ‎who doesn't like doctors doing here?

847
53:31.730 --> 53:32.897
‎I just got fired.

848
53:33.398 --> 53:34.315
‎I'm going home.

849
53:56.588 --> 53:58.256
‎What? She got fired?

850
53:59.591 --> 54:00.884
‎Ms. Han.

851
54:00.967 --> 54:03.261
‎But she saved a life. How could he--

852
54:05.305 --> 54:07.640
‎-Dr. Park. ‎-Forget it. Let's just eat.

853
54:08.683 --> 54:10.143
‎We said we'd be right back.

854
54:10.226 --> 54:13.146
‎Any experienced doctor ‎could do what she did.

855
54:13.229 --> 54:14.522
‎You're so right, Dr. Bae.

856
54:16.107 --> 54:17.358
‎One of my professors

857
54:17.442 --> 54:20.820
‎accidentally played a surgical video ‎at 1.5 times normal speed in class.

858
54:20.904 --> 54:22.155
‎Everyone laughed then.

859
54:22.238 --> 54:23.073
‎But…

860
54:23.573 --> 54:25.992
‎It's not funny if you're faster than that.

861
54:26.076 --> 54:28.286
‎Hey, you haven't seen enough surgeries.

862
54:28.369 --> 54:30.830
‎I could pull off a procedure like that ‎at that speed.

863
54:30.914 --> 54:31.790
‎Really?

864
54:32.499 --> 54:33.374
‎At that speed?

865
54:35.502 --> 54:37.295
‎You didn't watch ‎the video carefully, did you?

866
54:37.378 --> 54:38.922
‎You wouldn't know we switched gloves.

867
54:39.005 --> 54:41.174
‎I was called out because of them.

868
54:41.257 --> 54:42.842
‎She said to bring non-latex gloves.

869
54:43.927 --> 54:45.386
‎-Latex allergy? ‎-Latex allergy?

870
54:45.470 --> 54:46.679
‎Anaphylaxis.

871
54:46.763 --> 54:47.806
‎How did she know?

872
54:47.889 --> 54:50.266
‎His pre-op form ‎didn't mention a latex allergy.

873
54:50.350 --> 54:51.434
‎Rubber factory.

874
54:52.685 --> 54:55.480
‎But long-term rubber exposure ‎doesn't always lead to a delayed allergy--

875
54:55.563 --> 54:57.732
‎There was a strong enough allergen ‎to trigger a reaction.

876
54:57.816 --> 55:00.568
‎Wait a minute. So how did she know?

877
55:02.612 --> 55:04.948
‎How did she know ‎he was going to have a stroke?

878
55:06.491 --> 55:07.492
‎You don't think…

879
55:08.660 --> 55:10.411
‎she slipped him a drug, do you?

880
55:12.455 --> 55:14.415
‎Stop talking nonsense and just eat.

881
55:14.499 --> 55:15.875
‎She's gone now.

882
55:17.627 --> 55:21.840
‎The doctor saying irrational things ‎about drugging people keeps his job,

883
55:21.923 --> 55:23.967
‎while the one who saved a life gets fired.

884
55:24.050 --> 55:25.593
‎This hospital is a circus.

885
55:25.677 --> 55:28.763
‎That's enough. ‎We're hanging by a thread as it is.

886
55:28.847 --> 55:30.056
‎I also can't eat

887
55:30.723 --> 55:32.684
‎anything like this because of allergies.

888
55:45.280 --> 55:47.866
‎I'm relieved you're okay, Director Kim.

889
55:47.949 --> 55:50.243
‎So you saw it all, huh?

890
55:50.326 --> 55:52.328
‎Yes, I saw the whole thing.

891
55:53.288 --> 55:54.581
‎I was very concerned.

892
55:55.582 --> 55:56.666
‎No one seemed to know

893
55:56.749 --> 55:59.836
‎you went into anaphylactic shock.

894
55:59.919 --> 56:01.421
‎Anaphylaxis?

895
56:02.130 --> 56:03.298
‎How did you know?

896
56:03.381 --> 56:05.925
‎I stopped by your office ‎to say hello this morning,

897
56:06.009 --> 56:08.094
‎and saw your secretary ‎throw away some melon.

898
56:09.304 --> 56:13.224
‎And you kept scratching ‎the back of your neck in the OR.

899
56:14.434 --> 56:15.476
‎I'm sure you know

900
56:15.560 --> 56:20.106
‎delayed allergic reactions to latex ‎are common among healthcare workers.

901
56:20.190 --> 56:21.441
‎Latex?

902
56:21.524 --> 56:22.567
‎Director Kim.

903
56:24.611 --> 56:26.154
‎Why did you do it?

904
56:26.738 --> 56:28.990
‎Powdered gloves were banned by law

905
56:29.073 --> 56:32.535
‎because inhaling the particles ‎can cause anaphylactic shock.

906
56:34.162 --> 56:37.207
‎But you ignored that ‎for your own convenience.

907
56:40.293 --> 56:42.629
‎Your patient's life was at stake.

908
56:42.712 --> 56:45.173
‎No. I didn't--

909
56:45.256 --> 56:47.008
‎Of course, you didn't know.

910
56:47.091 --> 56:50.845
‎You didn't know that both you ‎and the patient had a latex allergy.

911
56:52.138 --> 56:53.932
‎Or that something ‎would trigger a reaction.

912
56:56.184 --> 56:58.686
‎How long have you been away from the OR

913
56:58.770 --> 57:00.813
‎not to know that?

914
57:03.066 --> 57:04.943
‎No, it's not in the footage.

915
57:05.568 --> 57:06.569
‎However…

916
57:12.075 --> 57:13.910
‎I have this.

917
57:25.338 --> 57:27.799
‎MAY EXACERBATE ‎LATEX-INDUCED ALLERGIC REACTIONS

918
57:27.882 --> 57:30.635
‎I heard you also received a box ‎from the locum tenens agency.

919
57:32.303 --> 57:34.597
‎Since the hospital pays ‎for temporary workers anyway,

920
57:34.681 --> 57:38.142
‎you got to line your own pockets ‎without spending a dime.

921
57:41.062 --> 57:43.690
‎I know, I know.

922
57:45.400 --> 57:46.568
‎Just breathe.

923
57:48.611 --> 57:49.737
‎I only want…

924
57:51.864 --> 57:52.865
‎one thing.

925
57:59.247 --> 58:00.164
‎Thank you.

926
58:04.335 --> 58:05.837
‎Thank you, Doctor.

927
58:16.931 --> 58:19.934
‎THE DIRECTOR WILL BE MAKING ROUNDS ‎PLEASE GET READY

928
58:27.900 --> 58:31.321
‎Director Bu Seung-gwon ‎will now begin rounds.

929
58:35.325 --> 58:36.159
‎Hello.

930
58:57.513 --> 58:59.807
‎DIRECTOR'S OFFICE

931
59:09.108 --> 59:12.278
‎I appreciate you requesting ‎Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

932
59:12.362 --> 59:13.196
‎Thank you.

933
59:15.657 --> 59:16.532
‎Director.

934
59:17.200 --> 59:20.161
‎Here is the new contract.

935
59:20.244 --> 59:21.079
‎Just a moment.

936
59:26.751 --> 59:27.919
‎EMPLOYMENT CONTRACT

937
59:28.002 --> 59:29.128
‎Oh my.

938
59:31.756 --> 59:33.883
‎Eight-hour workdays.

939
59:33.966 --> 59:35.301
‎Overtime comes with special pay.

940
59:35.385 --> 59:37.345
‎Surgeries come with per-case bonuses.

941
59:37.428 --> 59:38.554
‎Double pay for night shifts.

942
59:39.681 --> 59:41.265
‎Here's the rate sheet.

943
59:43.935 --> 59:44.977
‎Bonuses?

944
59:45.645 --> 59:46.646
‎Wait…

945
59:47.230 --> 59:49.190
‎This is higher than my salary.

946
59:50.149 --> 59:51.567
‎I can't accept this, sir.

947
59:51.651 --> 59:54.278
‎Why don't you join our agency then?

948
59:55.697 --> 59:58.199
‎Sir, if anything goes wrong ‎during surgery,

949
59:58.282 --> 59:59.701
‎it'll be entirely on us.

950
59:59.784 --> 01:00:02.912
‎Dr. Gye here will not do any work ‎that doesn't require

951
01:00:02.995 --> 01:00:04.372
‎a medical license.

952
01:00:04.455 --> 01:00:07.500
‎There's a lot of scut work ‎to do in hospitals.

953
01:00:07.583 --> 01:00:09.293
‎-That's why she-- ‎-Enough.

954
01:00:09.877 --> 01:00:12.088
‎For example, helping attendings ‎with their research.

955
01:00:12.171 --> 01:00:13.464
‎I don't do that.

956
01:00:13.548 --> 01:00:14.716
‎Pulling data for attendings.

957
01:00:14.799 --> 01:00:15.717
‎I don't do that.

958
01:00:15.800 --> 01:00:17.176
‎Director rounds, attending rounds.

959
01:00:17.260 --> 01:00:18.094
‎I don't do that.

960
01:00:18.177 --> 01:00:21.055
‎Work dinners, networking, ‎gatherings, making friendly overtures,

961
01:00:21.139 --> 01:00:22.807
‎talent shows, and more.

962
01:00:22.890 --> 01:00:24.142
‎I don't do any of that.

963
01:00:24.225 --> 01:00:25.226
‎It's all written there.

964
01:00:26.310 --> 01:00:27.603
‎SPECIAL TERMS

965
01:00:27.687 --> 01:00:29.522
‎I don't do any of that

966
01:00:30.481 --> 01:00:31.357
‎for any reason.

967
01:00:32.108 --> 01:00:33.234
‎What is this nonsense?

968
01:00:33.317 --> 01:00:35.111
‎What's important is that Dr. Gye…

969
01:00:35.194 --> 01:00:36.279
‎Failure?

970
01:00:38.364 --> 01:00:39.407
‎I don't do that either.

971
01:00:44.120 --> 01:00:45.121
‎Director.

972
01:00:45.204 --> 01:00:46.247
‎You start today.

973
01:00:46.831 --> 01:00:49.083
‎Thank you. You won't regret this.

974
01:00:51.544 --> 01:00:53.463
‎I look forward to ‎working with you, Dr. Gye.

975
01:00:56.340 --> 01:00:59.677
‎I don't do social niceties either.

976
01:00:59.761 --> 01:01:00.762
‎Why that…

977
01:01:03.681 --> 01:01:05.892
‎Did you put what I gave you to good use?

978
01:01:07.393 --> 01:01:08.895
‎Yes.

979
01:01:08.978 --> 01:01:10.980
‎Then we'll save that for next time.

980
01:01:12.857 --> 01:01:14.609
‎Have a good day, everyone.

981
01:01:14.692 --> 01:01:16.736
‎If you ever

982
01:01:16.819 --> 01:01:19.155
‎Become lonely

983
01:01:19.238 --> 01:01:20.156
‎Oh, wait.

984
01:01:21.199 --> 01:01:22.074
‎Just a minute!

985
01:01:28.080 --> 01:01:31.292
‎That person won't help you ‎build the future you want.

986
01:01:31.876 --> 01:01:33.961
‎She has an impressive resume.

987
01:01:34.045 --> 01:01:35.880
‎She'll be an asset to the hospital.

988
01:01:35.963 --> 01:01:37.965
‎But there are others with her experience--

989
01:01:38.049 --> 01:01:39.634
‎Did you watch the entire surgical video?

990
01:01:39.717 --> 01:01:40.551
‎Yes.

991
01:01:41.969 --> 01:01:45.556
‎I've never seen hands move that fast.

992
01:01:56.150 --> 01:01:58.152
‎There's someone else who should have this.

993
01:02:03.324 --> 01:02:07.119
‎Why are they bringing in that mad dog?

994
01:02:07.203 --> 01:02:08.204
‎This is insane.

995
01:02:18.089 --> 01:02:20.925
‎She hates belonging to a group ‎and despises authority.

996
01:02:26.264 --> 01:02:27.265
‎This person…

997
01:02:28.766 --> 01:02:31.143
‎could throw everything into turmoil.

998
01:02:33.896 --> 01:02:36.065
‎RESUME ‎NAME: GYE SU-JEONG

999
01:02:36.148 --> 01:02:36.983
‎Dr. Gye Su-jeong!

1000
01:02:41.404 --> 01:02:42.238
‎Oh, here.

1001
01:02:43.781 --> 01:02:46.158
‎I noticed your name ‎wasn't embroidered on it yet.

1002
01:02:58.254 --> 01:03:00.172
‎Oh, and I know about ‎melons and tropical fruit.

1003
01:03:00.756 --> 01:03:04.176
‎People with latex allergies ‎can react to tropical fruit too.

1004
01:03:23.279 --> 01:03:24.780
‎He runs a rubber factory.

1005
01:03:25.740 --> 01:03:28.159
‎No, bring me powdered gloves.

1006
01:03:28.242 --> 01:03:30.244
‎Her only weapons are her medical license

1007
01:03:30.745 --> 01:03:34.165
‎and the surgical skills ‎she has honed from the bottom up.

1008
01:03:34.790 --> 01:03:35.791
‎Dr. Gye Su-jeong!

1009
01:03:37.585 --> 01:03:38.586
‎Gye Su-jeong.

1010
01:03:39.712 --> 01:03:41.088
‎Will you answer for once?

1011
01:03:42.340 --> 01:03:43.257
‎Did you hear me?

1012
01:03:45.134 --> 01:03:46.510
‎Are you ignoring us?

1013
01:03:47.595 --> 01:03:49.513
‎Hey, Gye-snake!

1014
01:03:49.597 --> 01:03:51.140
‎Gye Su-jeong, the surgeon.

1015
01:03:52.266 --> 01:03:54.769
‎At the end of the day, she's disposable.

1016
01:03:56.520 --> 01:03:59.315
‎We can cut her loose ‎along with the hospital's other problems.

1017
01:04:01.734 --> 01:04:04.695
‎So let's just wait and see how she does.

1018
01:04:12.328 --> 01:04:14.372
‎Why did you come back ‎if you hate it so much?

1019
01:04:15.206 --> 01:04:17.625
‎Why did you become a doctor ‎if you hate it so much?

1020
01:04:20.878 --> 01:04:21.921
‎Also known as

1021
01:04:23.214 --> 01:04:24.966
‎Doctor X.

1022
01:05:04.380 --> 01:05:09.010
‎IN MEMORY OF KIM HYUN-I, ‎OUR CHERISHED COLLEAGUE

1023
01:05:09.093 --> 01:05:12.013
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

1024
01:05:12.680 --> 01:05:15.141
‎-"Mad dog"? ‎-‎You can't do it with your skills.

1025
01:05:15.224 --> 01:05:16.600
‎Are we really working with her?

1026
01:05:16.684 --> 01:05:17.977
‎She gets on my nerves.

1027
01:05:18.060 --> 01:05:19.437
‎Can I just not do the surgery?

1028
01:05:19.520 --> 01:05:21.772
‎-Objection. ‎-Are you saying you can do it?

1029
01:05:21.856 --> 01:05:23.941
‎Just let me die!

1030
01:05:24.025 --> 01:05:26.527
‎There's no difference ‎if you die today or next week.

1031
01:05:26.610 --> 01:05:29.238
‎She'll push ahead with surgery ‎no matter the risk to the patient.

1032
01:05:29.321 --> 01:05:30.531
‎Now it's starting to get fun.

1033
01:05:30.614 --> 01:05:32.992
‎You're bound to fail at some point.

1034
01:05:33.075 --> 01:05:34.618
‎You're a doctor!

1035
01:05:34.702 --> 01:05:36.287
‎You have a duty to save your patient!

1036
01:05:37.288 --> 01:05:42.293
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
